---
import researchHero from '~/assets/images/research.png';
import res from '~/assets/images/res.png';
---
<!-- HERO -->
<section
  class="relative h-[500px] flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden"
>
  <img
    src={researchHero.src}
    alt="Publications"
    class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-center"
  />

  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/50"></div>

  <div class="relative z-10 text-center px-6">
    <h1 class="text-white font-extrabold text-5xl md:text-7xl">
      Research
    </h1>

      
</section>

     <section class="bg-white py-12">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-8">

    <p class="text-xl leading-9 text-gray-700 text-justify">
        The <strong>CLab</strong>
        develops innovative synthetic strategies for the preparation of structurally
        diverse small molecules inspired by natural products and biologically relevant
        scaffolds. Our research integrates <strong>organic synthesis</strong>,
        <strong>medicinal chemistry</strong>, and
        <strong>computational chemistry</strong> to generate molecular libraries
        with potential applications in human health.
      </p>
      <img
  src={res.src}
  alt="Graphical abstract"
  class="mt-8 mx-auto max-w-xl"
/>
<div class="mt-8">
  <p class="text-xl leading-9 text-gray-700 text-justify">

    Our research integrates organic synthesis, medicinal chemistry, and computational chemistry to develop innovative molecular architectures with biological and therapeutic potential. We develop efficient synthetic strategies for the construction and diversification of complex molecules, combining function-oriented synthesis (FOS), skeletal editing, and cascade reactions with the design and optimization of bioactive compounds targeting diseases of high societal impact, particularly breast cancer, Alzheimer’s disease, and cardiovascular disorders. Computational approaches, including molecular docking, density functional theory (DFT), and transition-state (TS) calculations, complement our experimental studies by providing insights into reaction mechanisms and molecular recognition, while guiding the rational design of new molecules. Through the integration of molecular design, synthesis, biological evaluation, and computational analysis, CLab seeks to advance sustainable approaches to modern organic synthesis and accelerate the discovery of molecules with therapeutic potential.

  </p>
</div>
</section>